<title>PORTUGAL: Portucel hits high after price news.</title>
<headline>Portucel hits high after price news.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Portuguese pulp group Portucel Industrial hit an all-time high of 1,350 escudos after the company said it was raising Bleached Eucalyptus Kraft Pulp (BEKP) prices.</p>
<p>&quot;Portucel was high all morning, but surged to a new record after the price announcement,&quot; a dealer said.</p>
<p>Portucel said it was raising the price of BEKP by 40 ecus per tonne to 490 with effect from July 1.</p>
<p>Portucel shares later eased from the record high to 1,330 escudos, up 74, in volume of 694,547 at 1205 GMT.</p>
